      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I&#39;d say the Sentinels are the best call mechanics-wise, since they&#39;re so One-Shot dependent.&nbsp; Not sure how they line up flavor-wise, since they&#39;re mostly a pretty obscure group in-setting.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But now you&#39;ve gotten me wondering about characters like The Scholar and Chrono-Ranger, who probably <em>could</em> work in this format, but operating very differently (Ranger cares more about damaging One-Shots and less anout Equipment, Scholar is pushed towards Iron Form over Liquid Energy).&nbsp; I might just have to try that!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>ExPat is bad, but I&#39;d say Unity is the worst option in this format.&nbsp; With no Guns and no Golems, you&#39;ve got one character who can only play RPG Launcher and Flak Jacket, and another who can only play Brainstorm.&nbsp; Hoping to draw a second Brainstorm.&nbsp; Oh, and I guess Powered Shockwave, should there be a damage boost out.&nbsp; Sure, the Adept only has Vernal Sonata, but a few Vernal Sonatas can win games.&nbsp; And I guess there&#39;s always Silver Shadow to activate the odd Accompany.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So intriguing!&nbsp; I think I&#39;ll play my next game this way, using Tachyon, Sentinels, Scholar, and Legacy.&nbsp; I&#39;ll probably take the coward&#39;s path and start with someone easy like Ambuscade, then if that goes well, move on to the serious villains.</p>",
