      "raw": "<p>Okay, played a couple of games.&nbsp; The first one was, as planned, against Ambuscade.&nbsp; I chose Freedom Tower, which seemed like a good place to hold a press conference.&nbsp; Ultimately, the game was a bit of a farce - the Tower ended up putting a bunch of Hero Ongoings/Equipment into&nbsp; play, and Ambuscade has no stuff destruction, so we wore him down in a slow game which never really felt in question.</p><p>Clearly, I needed a tougher villain with a woder range of threats - but anyone <em>too</em> fast would probably just kill everyone before their stunted setup could work.&nbsp; Also, an environment which did damage could be more interesting.&nbsp; So, Tachyon opened Cretaceus World, and called the Sentinels, Legacy, and the Scholar (as well as those pesky members of the press) to tour the facilities.&nbsp; Inevitably, they got attacked by Egyptian gods.</p><p>Okay, so the story&#39;s a little odd there, but the Ennead (non-Advanced) play relatively slowly, but can still be a threat and dish out some Ongoing/Equipment disruption.&nbsp; It was a brutal match - and I got lucky, never seeing the extra card play Ennead members.&nbsp; Over twelve turns, Legacy and the Scholar locked them down whilst Tachyon and the Sentinels took them out.&nbsp; I&#39;d recommend this game for anyone looking to try a unique challenge - though Insula Primalis for the Environment may be a bit much.</p>",
